WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.830
In 2013, UNESCO listed a way of
eating as intangible heritage:

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.530
Washoku, traditional
Japanese dietary culture.

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.270
In Fujian, in southeast China, a whole
clan could share one round earthen house:

4
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.010
a tulou.

5
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:21.150
In the Philippines, the Ifugao rice
terraces follow the mountain contours.

6
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.350
UNESCO's listing says they
have done so for 2,000 years.

7
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.770
Which one is normal?

8
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.410
What most people do?

9
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.970
What experts say?

10
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.630
Who decides which foods, homes
and customs count as normal?

11
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.610
In this mission, you'll
find out what culture is,

12
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.010
and how it is handed from
one generation to the next.

13
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.270
Then you'll meet two attitudes
geographers can take to other cultures.

14
00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.790
Your mission: decide who
gets to say which foods,

15
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.230
homes and customs count as normal.
